-- title:
--   Theorem 2.1 — the hyperplane projection method converges to a solution of $\mathrm{VI}(F, C)$
-- statement:
--   Let $C$ be a closed convex subset of $\mathbb{R}^n$ and $F : \mathbb{R}^n \to \mathbb{R}^n$ continuous. Suppose that the solution set $S$ of the variational inequality $\mathrm{VI}(F, C)$ is nonempty and that condition (1.2) holds:
--
--   $$\langle F(x), x - x^* \rangle \ge 0 \qquad \text{for all } x \in C \text{ and all } x^* \in S.$$
--
--   Let $\gamma, \sigma \in (0,1)$. Then every sequence $(x^i)$ generated by Algorithm 2.1 converges to a solution of $\mathrm{VI}(F, C)$: there is $\hat x \in S$ with
--
--   $$\lim_{i \to \infty} x^i = \hat x.$$
--
--   The theorem requires neither Lipschitz continuity nor monotonicity of $F$; condition (1.2) holds for pseudomonotone maps and more generally. Each iteration of the method needs only one projection onto $C$ and one onto $C \cap H_i$.
--
--   **Formalization Note** $\mathbb{R}^n$ is `EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)`; projections are `projOnto`, which is the true projection on the nonempty closed convex sets the algorithm uses. A run that stops at a solution ($r(x^i) = 0$) is continued as a constant sequence (the stall encoding of `IsAlg21Run`), so finitely terminating runs are included and converge trivially. The whole sequence is required to converge to a single solution.
-- source:
--   Solodov & Svaiter, A New Projection Method for Variational Inequality Problems, SIAM J. Control Optim. 37 (1999), p. 769, Theorem 2.1

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_SolodovSvaiterVI_Alg21_viSol
import Definitions.Def_SolodovSvaiterVI_Alg21_SatisfiesCond12
import Definitions.Def_SolodovSvaiterVI_Alg21_IsAlg21Run

namespace SolodovSvaiterVI.Alg21

/-- Theorem 2.1 of Solodov–Svaiter (p. 769): let `C ⊆ ℝⁿ` be closed and convex and `F`
continuous; suppose the solution set `S` of `VI(F, C)` is nonempty and condition (1.2) holds.
Then any sequence `{xⁱ}` generated by Algorithm 2.1 (parameters `γ, σ ∈ (0, 1)`) converges to
a solution of `VI(F, C)`.

**Formalization Note.** A run that stops at a solution is continued as a constant sequence
(stall encoding, see `IsAlg21Run`); `P_K` is `projOnto K`. -/
theorem theorem2_1_converges_to_solution {n : ℕ}
    (F : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))
    (C : Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))) (hCc : IsClosed C) (hCcv : Convex ℝ C)
    (hF : Continuous F) (hS : (viSol F C).Nonempty) (h12 : SatisfiesCond12 F C)
    (gamma sigma : ℝ) (hγ0 : 0 < gamma) (hγ1 : gamma < 1) (hσ0 : 0 < sigma) (hσ1 : sigma < 1)
    (x : ℕ → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)) (k : ℕ → ℕ) (hrun : IsAlg21Run F C gamma sigma x k) :
    ∃ xs ∈ viSol F C, Filter.Tendsto x Filter.atTop (nhds xs) := by sorry

end SolodovSvaiterVI.Alg21
